 "section_summary": "This section comprises U.S. diplomatic correspondence and State Department memoranda from late December 1938 through early April 1939, centered on the Tokyo Embassy's comprehensive monthly political reports for January (Report No. 148) and February (Report No. 149). The documents record the installation of the Hiranuma Cabinet, expanding state control under the National General Mobilization Law, and escalating Japanese military actions in China, including the occupation of Hainan Island and tensions in Shanghai. They also document extensive American and British diplomatic protests regarding treaty rights, trade restrictions, property destruction, the integrity of the Chinese Maritime Customs, and navigation on the Yangtze River.",
