   "summary": "Ambassador Grew transmits Report No. 149 covering conditions in Japan during February 1939, with the first 17 pages of the report included in this section. The Embassy lodged extensive protests regarding Japanese naval trade restrictions at Chefoo, interference with the Chinese Maritime Customs, restrictions in Tientsin, shipping on the Yangtze, safety of Americans in Kuling, and numerous mission bombings in China. Internationally, the report analyzes the military and strategic significance of Japan's occupation of Hainan Island, escalating terrorist assassinations in Shanghai prompting Japanese demands against the Municipal Council, military campaigns across Hopei and Shantung, and an accidental Japanese aerial bombing of Hong Kong territory settled via apology and indemnification.",
